--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[class.union]/2: a union may have a user-declared constructor and is then
constructed via that constructor (not by conversion).  This is the storage
shape of std::optional/std::variant (a union with a constructor that initialises
one member).  Copy-assignment of such a (non-POD) union is a separate, still-open
issue (the implicit operator= parameter type does not resolve); construction and
copy-construction work.

